1. [NAME] Docs: Introduction
---

This is the documentation for [NAME], the GPU compute cluster for the infectious disease epidemiology department. The docs will just be pure text files that are fed into `less` viewer (`man less` for more details). The style is similar to markdown files with the following notation:

* ` - backticks denote commands you can type, 3 backticks denote a code block
  Examples:
  This is the `ls` command in a sentence, while the following is a code block:
  ```
  ls
  cd dir
  ```

* > - indicates what the command will print
  Examples:
  ```
  echo hello
  > hello
  ```
  Note that many outputs of commands are ommited. Only those whose outputs are relevant to the point are shown in these docs.

* (!) - this symbol is important information
  Examples:
  (!) Please don't ignore me

* * - asterisk symbol emphasises a word
  Examples:
  Green is *not* a creative colour

